"2026-11-13","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land — Plains"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Snow-Covered Island","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {U}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["U"],"released_at":"2021-02-05","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Snow Land — Island"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"banned","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"banned","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"banned","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"banned","vintage":"restricted"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}","name":"Sol Ring","oracle_id":"6ad8011d-3471-4369-9d68-b264cc027487","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}{C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"banned","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"banned","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{G}","name":"Veil of Summer","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","oracle_text":"Draw a card if an opponent has cast a blue or black spell this turn. Spells you control can't be countered this turn. You and permanents you control gain hexproof from blue and from black until end of turn. (You and they can't be the targets of blue or black spells or abilities your opponents control.)","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2019-07-12","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"A spell or ability that counters spells can still target your spells after Veil of Summer resolves. When that spell or ability resolves, your spell won't be countered, but any additional effects of the countering spell or ability will still happen.","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If your opponents have cast more than one blue or black spell, you still draw only one card as Veil of Summer resolves.","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Veil of Summer has no effect until it resolves. It can be countered.","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.","oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Arcane is a spell subtype that has no inherent rules meaning. It may be referenced by effects from other cards.","oracle_id":"2837888c-bfa8-4955-9334-0605ad409f7e","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell is not countered (because the spell it targets can't be countered), then it does not get exiled.","oracle_id":"4b2e9aa9-6f91-41de-84b6-e9a89be06a53","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The card does not go to the graveyard before being exiled.","oracle_id":"4b2e9aa9-6f91-41de-84b6-e9a89be06a53","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In a Limited event (usually Booster Draft or Sealed Deck), you can't add basic snow lands to your card pool as you would other basic lands. You can play with basic snow lands only if you open them in your sealed deck or draft them.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Snow is a supertype, not a card type. It has no rules meaning or function by itself, but spells and abilities may refer to it.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Snow isn't a type of mana. If an effect says you may spend mana as though it were any type, you can't pay for {S} using mana that wasn't produced by a snow source.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some cards have additional effects for each {S} spent to cast them. You can cast these spells even if you don't spend any snow mana to cast them; their additional effects simply won't do anything.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The Kaldheim set doesn't have any cards with mana costs that include {S}, but some previous sets do. If an effect says such a spell costs {1} less to cast, that reduction doesn't apply to any {S} costs. This is also true for activated abilities that include {S} in their activation costs and effects that reduce those costs.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The {S} symbol is a generic mana symbol. It represents a cost that can be paid by one mana that was produced by a snow source. That mana can be any color or colorless.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An effect that instructs you to \"cast\" a card doesn't allow you to play lands.","oracle_id":"d5be0ff6-39d9-4f9f-a028-e62dc38463f2","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Casting the card causes it to leave exile. You can't cast it multiple times.","oracle_id":"d5be0ff6-39d9-4f9f-a028-e62dc38463f2","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gonti doesn't change when you can cast the exiled card. For example, if you exile a creature card without flash, you can cast it only during your main phase when the stack is empty.","oracle_id":"d5be0ff6-39d9-4f9f-a028-e62dc38463f2","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you leave the game, the card remains exiled face down indefinitely. No player may look at it.","oracle_id":"d5be0ff6-39d9-4f9f-a028-e62dc38463f2","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may look at and cast that card (and spend mana as though it were mana of any type to do so) even if Gonti leaves the battlefield. If another player gains control of Gonti, that player can't look at or cast the card, and you still can.","oracle_id":"d5be0ff6-39d9-4f9f-a028-e62dc38463f2","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You pay the costs for the exiled card if you cast it. You may pay alternative costs such as emerge rather than the card's mana cost.","oracle_id":"d5be0ff6-39d9-4f9f-a028-e62dc38463f2","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The six types of mana are white, blue, black, red, green, and colorless. Snow mana is not a type of mana. Gonti, Lord of Luxury won't let you pay a snow cost using mana produced by a nonsnow source.","oracle_id":"d5be0ff6-39d9-4f9f-a028-e62dc38463f2","published_at":"2023-07-28","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
